# Motion Primitives

For React UI animations in Doxa, prefer **[Motion Primitives](https://motion-primitives.com)** the same way we prefer **shadcn/ui** for primitives.

## Source of truth

- Docs / catalog: https://motion-primitives.com/docs
- Installation: https://motion-primitives.com/docs/installation
- GitHub: https://github.com/ibelick/motion-primitives
- Runtime dependency: `motion` (already in root `package.json`)

## How to add a component

1. Prefer the CLI (copies owned source into the repo):

```bash
npx motion-primitives@latest add <component-name>
```

Example: `npx motion-primitives@latest add text-effect`

2. Or copy from the docs page into [`components/motion-primitives/`](components/motion-primitives/).

Do **not** invent one-off Framer/Motion wrappers when a Motion Primitive already covers the interaction (text effects, in-view reveals, morphing dialogs, infinite sliders, spotlight, tilt, etc.).

## Conventions

- Keep copied components under `components/motion-primitives/` (CLI default).
- Customize copied source to match Doxa tokens (`app/globals.css`, neumorphic panel language)—same ownership model as shadcn under `components/ui/`.
- Use existing `cn` from `@/lib/utils`; do not add a second utils helper for motion components.
- Prefer purposeful motion that supports hierarchy and presence. Avoid decorative noise, endless loops on dense admin surfaces, and purple/glow demos that fight the design system.
- shadcn/ui remains the default for non-animated primitives (Button, Dialog shell, forms, etc.). Compose: shadcn structure + Motion Primitive motion where helpful.
- **Text fields:** `components/ui/input.tsx` and `textarea.tsx` always use `SpotlightBorder` (`--accent-primary` gradient) on focus. Do not reintroduce `focus-visible:ring-ring` / accent border rings on those primitives. Use `@/components/ui/input` and `@/components/ui/textarea` instead of raw `<input>` / `<textarea>` for text fields.

## When not to use it

- Pipeline / agents / Supabase Edge / workers — no UI animation stack there.
- Data-heavy tables and critical admin workflows — keep motion minimal or none.
